From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:02:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Horizon on Linux: layered, 3D and mip-mapped textures, views,
 copies, stencil, input

Textures keep all their levels and layers (2D arrays, cube maps, 3D), sampled through views of the
type the shader asks for, and render targets may be a layer, a face or a slice (texture views are
recorded). Buffer to texture and texture to texture copies, depth and stencil state, blend constants,
depth bias, indirect draws and the depth clip convention are made. Uploads go through the ring without
waiting. Shaders translate in the translator's debug mode (all 3867 of Xenoblade Chronicles 2's).
horizon_input.py feeds the window's keys and gamepad to NpadState, NX2LINUX_PRESS scripts presses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NX2Linux S7bis: layered, 3D and mip-mapped textures, copies, stencil and input for the Vulkan GPU path
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

